<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs flat to weak in New York as Dow falls.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs flat to weak in New York as Dow falls.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were flat to weaker in afternoon New York trade, where the Dow Industrials was 20.78 down at 6675.7 at 7.45 a.m. NZT.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$31 1/2	 -0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$28 7/8	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 3/4	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$15 1/8	 -0 3/8 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$82 1/4	 -0 7/8 *</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  35		    nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  186		 + 1/2</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  243		 -0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  149 1/4	   -0 1/2</p>
<p>Templeton	London  144 1/2	   -0 3/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.21		-10</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.61		-1</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.56		-4</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
